<%# PREVIEW - the worst case for merging view and edit, and the one that shows why the merge is a
    simplification rather than a rearrangement.

    **Eight read-only cards became two sections.** The old page rendered Description, Price information,
    Company information, Financial metrics, Industry averages, Management, Competitor names and Portfolio
    stocks. The edit form edits **every one of those attributes** - seventeen fields including both prices - so
    six of the eight cards were the form's own fields displayed a second time, on a different page, where they
    could not be changed. Nothing was lost by deleting them; the fields *are* the display now.

    What genuinely is not editable is the **derived** figure - the percentage change, computed from the two
    prices - and the **collection** of portfolios holding the stock. The first is a glanceable summary, so it
    goes in the header beside the price; the second is a section of its own.

    **Order follows what the page is for, while the shape stays fixed.** On a school the collection leads,
    because managing years is why you open it. On a stock the fundamentals lead, because editing them is. The
    shared partial fixes the column, the header and the section grammar; it does not fix the order. %>
<%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_page",
           locals: { title: @stock.company_name.presence || @stock.ticker,
                     breadcrumbs: @breadcrumbs,
                     description: stock_price_summary(@stock),
                     actions: capture do
                       link_to "Delete stock", admin_stock_path(@stock),
                               data: { turbo_method: :delete, turbo_confirm: delete_confirm(@stock) },
                               class: admin_danger_button_class
                     end } do %>
  <%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_section",
             locals: { title: "Details",
                       hint: "Grouped as they were on the old read-only cards. Saved when you press " \
                             "Save changes." } do %>
    <%= render "form" %>
  <% end %>

  <%# The one thing the form cannot express: who holds it. Read-only because an admin does not assign a
      holding - a student buys it. %>
  <%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_section", locals: { title: "Held by" } do %>
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
      <% if @stock.portfolio_stocks.any? %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-900">
          Held in <%= pluralize(@stock.portfolio_stocks.count, "portfolio") %>.
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">No student holds this stock yet.</p>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
